CT~~CD,~CC^~CT~
^XA
~TA000
~JSN
^MMT
^MPE
~SD20
^JZY
^MFN,N
^XZ

; =====================================================================
; CH0204 ROUND LABEL - HYBRID (native Data Matrix + curved-text graphic)
; 0.443 in dia round | 600 dpi | Thermal Transfer | black-mark media
; Data Matrix data = N0000   |  curved text = CH0204-0000
; SEND RAW (not through the ZDesigner graphics driver).
; NOTE: comment lines must NOT contain a caret, or the printer reads it
; as a command. That is why commands are written plainly below (LH, BX...).
; =====================================================================

; ---- 1) Media config (mark sensing, TT, size) + SAVE --------------
^XA
^MNM,0
^MTT
^PMN
^LL362
^PW400
^LH0,0
^LS0
^JUS
^XZ

; ---- 2) The label ------------------------------------------------
^XA
^PW400
^LL362
;
; ========== POSITION KNOB: edit the LH numbers on the next line =====
; LH x,y moves the WHOLE design.  x bigger = RIGHT.  y bigger = DOWN.
; Default puts the design as high as the current calibration allows.
; If the TOP of the ring prints cut off even at y=0, the print-start is
; too late - re-run media calibration (see notes at bottom).
; ==================================================================
^LH141,4
;
; --- curved text ring CH0204-0000 (graphic) ---
^FO0,0^GFA,5221,5221,23,^FS
;
; --- native Data Matrix, data = N0000 (edit the FD data to vary serial) ---
^FO174,85^BXN,4,200^FDN0000^FS
^XZ

; =====================================================================
; NOTES
; - Data Matrix is native BX (module=4 dots, 12x12 symbol). Scannable.
; - The curved number is BAKED INTO the ring graphic. To change the serial
;   you must regenerate that graphic; the barcode (N0000) changes by
;   editing the FD data on the barcode line above.
; - Design centered horizontally at x=252 (your validated center).
; - Vertical: at your crosshair center y=83 the top of the ring falls above
;   the printable area, so it is placed at the highest printable spot.
;   For true vertical centering, recalibrate so the label top edge = y0:
;   Home - Tools - Print Quality - Calibrate Media (mark sensor over mark).
; =====================================================================
